


The hstr_clean function "hstr_clean.h"

            The hstr_clean function "hstr_clean.h" function
            clears the last byte of the array of size
            HSTR_SIZE_MAX that starts at the location
            specified by #0, "the array." Then clears the
            bytes from the end of the string whose initial
            character is at the location specified by #0
            through the end of the array.
